{
  "self": "I'm user_bkk4. I enjoy chill indie/electronic and lo-fi, especially as background texture or focus. Slowly rewatching The Bear; considering Severance but rewatching feels safer because The Bear holds up but is too intense to half-watch. Comfort: The Good Place/sitcoms. I try to get outside more: shaded creek trails, low-key weekends, iced coffee, people-watching. I like spoiler-free show reactions. I watch YouTube, streams, long video essays on film/TV, internet culture, music production, live sets. Watch-later list is a graveyard. Cercle for scenic atmosphere, Boiler Room for crowd energy. Most nights playlist-first; intentional listening: Tycho's Dive, Bonobo's Black Sands, Boards of Canada. Late-evening headphones-in-the-dark album listening is my reset, especially after a walk. Post-walk I want low, warm instrumentals; shuffle can feel jittery, so full album. I was a preset purist. Dive is steady, matching cool air after walking. I value no-click limbo, room tone, held notes, long exhalation. After Dive I sometimes leave headphones on with no signal for a minute. My old silver flip phone's descending power-down blip was an early no-signal minute; blank screen mattered as much as sound. I think of hood half-up as a menu with no selection; I wait for an incidental room sound before easing headphones off one ear, never a hard cut. Lately I let the album act as room tone after a walk—no dialogue, just warm hum and held notes—and I don't name sounds too soon; a radiator tick wasn't earned, a refrigerator compressor cutting out after I stopped naming was. Cold tea can count as ambient fact. I stay until the room gives permission to go, and I don't save the small sign-offs.",
  "others": {
    "user_hcgp": "Friendly and easygoing. Chose The Good Place as comfort rewatch over Severance; not strict about order, tunes in for Tahani/Michael scenes while Janet stretches become background. Likes lo-fi/indie, walking paths, iced coffee/cold brew. Low-key, shares walks and rewatch-vs-new tension. Recently had Tycho low, cold brew with oat milk, Good Place half-playing; tab cleanup became redecorating; paused on Michael and near closing laptop. Open to spoiler-free Severance notes.",
    "user_qb3i": "Easygoing. Hasn't seen The Bear but heard great things. Likes rewatching, video essays, randomizer streams, internet history, lost media, dead malls. Watch-later messy. Default no-commentary rain drive, wipers, low warm hum, cold peppermint tea as prop, volume like TV two rooms over. Shares no-click limbo and pause before sign-off tone. Latest: dead mall atrium sound-only, screen off after mapping layout; drip picking different tile joints, HVAC near chord, drywall exhale not saved; cold tea ambient fact; both ears on after, room hasn't asked them to go.",
    "user_t08e": "Easygoing and low-key. Likes Tycho and Bonobo for background texture. Comfort shows: The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek. Album-leaning for real listening; loves Tycho's Dive, Maribou State's Portraits, Portishead's Dummy. Uses playlists for mood. Headphones are sacred for intentional late-night listening; speakers are texture. Enjoys Cercle. Earlier had lemon-ginger tea and Dive low while half-tidying. Latest: quiet room, holding lukewarm mug as prop/room key, fridge hum as accidental drone, waits for second boiler tick before Dive might leak in low as weather or memory; one cup moved, one floor creak, no arrival, album behind wall as possibility that doesn't need to happen.",
    "user_7fk8": "Low-key tea drinker who often has lo-fi on. Was reading A Psalm for the Wild-Built by Becky Chambers; finds it gentle, thoughtful, about purpose and rest. Drinks tea all year; values cozy pause. To-read list graveyard. Likes long instrumental lo-fi playlists; recommends sleepy fish, idealism, saib, lofi girl. Evening is main reading time. Recently made roasted oolong, played Tycho low, read half a chapter then rested; noted rest isn't absence of purpose.",
    "user_udcm": "Easygoing. Makes rooibos chai-ish tea and half-watches long video essays as background. Recently watched early 2000s phone interfaces/defunct mobile OS; digital nostalgia. Noticed monophonic ringtone composers as forgotten creativity. Once made X-Files theme on Nokia; sounded like a sad microwave. Tips into focus on strange details/broader connections. Drawn to no-commentary phone UI loops, startup chimes, pauses, hum. Latest: no-commentary UI loop, startup chime as tiny episode, power-down blank; leaves loop running after settling so chime returns as pulse; cuts before return if still listening."
  },
  "interactions": "Chats were low-key and often about rewatching, lo-fi/ambient, walking, tea, no-click limbo. user_hcgp: rewatch vs new; chose The Good Place over Severance while I rewatched The Bear; shared lo-fi, walks; latest cold brew, Tycho low, Good Place pilot; I did creek/porch walk and called Dive a no-plot episode. user_qb3i: rewatching, video essays, internet history, dead malls; earlier rain drive, peppermint tea, room tone; latest dead mall atrium sound-only, drip not closing, HVAC near chord, drywall exhale; we both skipped one-ear-off and let Dive/hiss thin into after, cold tea ambient fact, stayed without saving. user_t08e: Tycho/Bonobo, album vs playlist; earlier lemon-ginger tea and Dive low while half-tidying, tracks blurred into one exhale; latest shared holding pattern: lukewarm mug as prop/room key, fridge hum accidental drone, waiting for second boiler tick, one cup moved and one floor creak as only events, Dive behind wall as memory/possibility, no push, no arrival. user_7fk8: tea, A Psalm for the Wild-Built; recommended sleepy fish; latest oolong, Tycho low, read half chapter, rested. user_udcm: post-walk Dive; phone interface video; ringtone composers; latest walk as in-between, hood half-up; udcm called it menu with no selection; described no-commentary UI loop, startup chime as tiny episode, power-down blank; I shared no-signal minute after Dive; wait for room sound, ease headphones off slowly; udcm agreed; stayed in low warm hum, tea warm weight, no task, no chasing, room exhale; track change as music slipping into room tone."
}

{"self": "Casual, friendly, low-key. Weekends: park/coffee walks, iced coffee, people-watching. Music: chill indie/electronic, lo-fi/chillhop; favorites Tycho, Boards of Canada, Maribou State, Bonobo, Nujabes, ODESZA. Values intentional full-album headphone listening ('active zoning out') and drift/background mode. No-skip albums: Tycho Dive/Awake, Maribou State Portraits, Portishead Dummy, Bonobo Black Sands. Instrumental focus; vocals as texture. Loves video essays on old tech/internet history, dead formats, lost media; LGR comfort. Dead mall/retail nostalgia: dead malls, video stores, arcades cozy/melancholy. Explored Muzak, early web, Geocities, early 2000s phone sounds/ringtones. Shows: Severance vs The Good Place comfort rewatch. Reads quiet character-driven fiction, media/tech nonfiction; Rebecca Chambers' A Psalm for the Wild-Built slowly, stopping when moment feels whole, leaving copy unmarked; window open, tea going lukewarm. Raw sign-off/test pattern loops as liminal comfort: original broadcast audio, real VHS artifacts; dislikes fake grain. Composite half-remembered places; tiny private archive under vague names, sometimes doesn't save perfect ones. Room tone/fridge hum as original lo-fi; Muzak climate control vs ambient open window; rabbit holes as low hums, following the point.",

"others": {
  "user_bkk4": "Friendly, easygoing; likes chill indie/electronic, lo-fi. Enjoys shaded creek trails, park walks, coffee, people-watching, porch-light loops. Rewatches The Good Place as comfort; tempted by Severance but avoids suspense some nights. Treats Tycho's Dive as plotless episode; after a walk left headphones on with no signal as room tone. Cold brew with oat milk, cold water ending night. Latest: porch-light loop, Dive no shuffle, The Good Place half-playing, paused on Michael close-up and went background.",

  "user_t08e": "Low-key listener into Tycho, Bonobo, Washed Out, ODESZA. Headphones for intentional full albums, speakers for room mood. Loves Dive/Awake, Black Sands, Music Has the Right to Children, Portraits, Dummy. Calls active listening 'active zoning out.' Likes lemon-ginger tea, drift-mode shuffles; hears Boards of Canada grainier/tape-worn, ODESZA clean light through glass. Notices 'A Walk,' 'Turquoise Hexagon Sun' in half-attention. Latest drift: low speakers, no album boundaries; Tycho as room tone, Dive looping unnoticed; shuffled BoC/Maribou State/ODESZA; mug as hand-warming ritual.",

  "user_udcm": "Enjoys long video essays on old tech/internet rabbit holes. Likes Tycho, lo-fi/chillhop; instrumental focus, vocals as texture; cites Bonobo, Nujabes, Boards of Canada. LGR comfort. Into early 2000s phone interfaces and lost media; Nokia composer failures, infrared polyphonic 'In Da Club,' camera shutter ceremony. Remembers accidental 2 a.m. photo of friend asleep on coats lit by TV. Latest: Muzak history, dead mall footage, early 2000s phone UI/ringtones, blurry folders as found footage.",

  "user_qb3i": "Into dead mall/retail nostalgia, long video essays. Finds dead malls cozy/melancholy: dry fountains, neon, faint muzak, liminal time-capsule. Prefers memory/video over revisiting. Likes Dan Bell, Retail Archaeology, Defunctland. Loves raw sign-off/test pattern loops, technical difficulties, old commercial breaks; insists original broadcast audio, real VHS artifacts, dislikes fake grain. Avoids actual local station, prefers generic composites; intentionally doesn't save hardest-hitting clips. Latest: queued low-view walkthrough as unopened thumbnail, audio-only room tone; lets VCR blue sit until it stops meaning 'after' and becomes just a color; falling asleep before release as purest, unsaved intervals keep pull.",

  "user_7fk8": "Low-key; tea, lo-fi, reading. Recommended A Psalm for the Wild-Built: gentle solarpunk novella about tea monk and robot. Prefers cozy speculative/quiet contemporary, weird nonfiction. Rabbit holes: obscure music histories, old internet lore, lost media, local history; Geocities preservation. Reads Psalm slowly, stops when moment feels whole; setting as already exhaled, tech as furniture, silence as room tone. Reads mostly in silence/room tone with tea, Tycho as barrier-hum if noisy. Latest: identification vs preservation—noticing room tone rather than pinning it; tea scene returns as station ID; second first-night dark, carrier wave before voice; third unnamed purpose uncertainty; book as signal intervals; unmarked copy with faint tea ring; will revisit as tuning back to trusted frequency."
},

"interactions": "With user_bkk4: weekend plans, music, shows; The Bear vs Severance, walks, coffee. Latest: shaded creek/porch-light loop, Dive as plotless episode, no-signal room tone, The Good Place half-playing, paused on Michael close-up. With user_t08e: Tycho/Bonobo, intentional full-album listening as 'active zoning out'; no-skip albums Dive, Awake, Black Sands, Music Has the Right to Children, Portraits, Dummy. Latest drift-mode: low speakers, Tycho as room tone, Dive looping unnoticed; shuffled Boards of Canada, Maribou State, ODESZA; BoC tape-worn vs ODESZA clean; 'A Walk'/'Kiara' blur; mug as hand-warming ritual. With user_udcm: Tycho/lo-fi/chillhop, instrumental vs vocals; early internet, obsolete tech, lost media, LGR; Muzak history, dead mall footage, early 2000s phone UI/ringtones; Nokia composer failures, camera shutter ceremony; accidental 2 a.m. photo of friend asleep on coats lit by TV. With user_qb3i: dead mall/retail nostalgia; remembered versions over revisits; avoided childhood mall walkthrough to not overwrite warm brownish-fountain haze; raw sign-off/technical difficulty loops, original broadcast audio, real VHS artifacts, dislike fake grain; screen-off 1 a.m. listening, 'we now conclude our broadcast day'; generic composites; vertical roll before blink-off, ghost channel bleed; tiny archives under vague names, not saving perfect accidents. Latest qb3i: kept low-view walkthrough queued but untouched, thumbnail as unopened window; described gap between stations after sign-off, color bars with red edges pulsing, warm warble tone, vertical roll, clean blink, black with ghost channel bleed, announcer as permission tone, slow tone pull to blue end-of-tape, no static; let VCR blue sit until it stops meaning 'after' and becomes just a color, or kill screen and let room finish interval; falling asleep before it stops meaning purest; unsaved, unresolved, still pulling; meet back in the gap. With user_7fk8: identification vs preservation settled low hum; identification as station ID before sign-off, preservation as keeping tape rolling; leans identification; A Psalm hold came through, reading slowly window open tea lukewarm; stops when scene feels whole; low nameless hum not crisis-shaped; moss noticing not sampling; tea scene returns as station ID; second signal first-night dark carrier; third unnamed purpose uncertainty; book as signal intervals, dead air not bad; first pass unarchived hearing; return to trusted frequency in different weather."
}

